{"name":"Sakura Panic","hex":"#ffb7c5","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sakura","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Japanese) cherry tree","cherry blossom (blossom of the Japanese cherry tree)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sakura"},{"term":"panic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Panic (“pertaining to the Greek god Pan”).","Of fear, fright, etc: overwhelming or sudden."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Overwhelming fear or fright, often affecting groups of people or animals;  an instance of this; a fright, a scare.","Ellipsis of kernel panic (“on Unix-derived operating systems: an action taken by the operating system when it cannot recover from a fatal error”);  any computer system crash."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry blossom","blocks":[{"text":"The cherry blossom, or sakura, is the flower of trees in Prunus subgenus Cerasus. Sakura usually refers to flowers of ornamental cherry trees, such as cultivars of Prunus serrulata, not trees grown for their fruit. Cherry blossoms have been described as having a vanilla-like smell, which is mainly attributed to coumarin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_blossom","wikidata":"Q871991"},{"title":"Panic","blocks":[{"text":"Panic is a sudden sensation of fear, which is so strong as to dominate or prevent reason and logical thinking, replacing it with overwhelming feelings of anxiety, uncertainty and frantic agitation consistent with a fight-or-flight reaction. Panic may occur singularly in individuals or manifest suddenly in large groups as mass panic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/The_expression_of_the_emotions_in_man_and_animals_%281872%29_%2814785143685%29.jpg/330px-The_expression_of_the_emotions_in_man_and_animals_%281872%29_%2814785143685%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail